## Query rules

- Replace `@PERIOD_DAYS` with the numeric lookback period before executing.
- If user supplies explicit dates, replace relative predicates with bounded start/end date predicates.
- Keep each query as one bounded read-only `SELECT TOP N` query.
- Do not use `SET DATEFIRST`; use `DATENAME(WEEKDAY, ...) NOT IN ('Saturday', 'Sunday')` for weekday filtering.
- If one query fails, show the error, note it in the report, and continue to the next query.

## Query 1 - Team-wide metrics

```sql
SELECT TOP 1
    COUNT(*) AS [Total Closed],
    CAST(ROUND(100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN DATEDIFF(HOUR, f.dateoccured, f.datecleared) <= 24 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0), 1) AS DECIMAL(5,1)) AS [% Closed in 24h],
    CAST(ROUND(100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN DATEDIFF(HOUR, f.dateoccured, f.datecleared) <= 48 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0), 1) AS DECIMAL(5,1)) AS [% Closed in 48h],
    CAST(ROUND(100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN apt.AppointmentCount < 5 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0), 1) AS DECIMAL(5,1)) AS [% < 5 Appts],
    CAST(ROUND(100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN apt.AppointmentCount = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0), 1) AS DECIMAL(5,1)) AS [% FCR]
FROM faults f
CROSS APPLY (
    SELECT COUNT(*) AS AppointmentCount
    FROM Appointment a2
    WHERE a2.APFaultid = f.Faultid
      AND a2.APdeleted = 0
) apt
WHERE f.fdeleted = 0
  AND f.Status IN (8, 9)
  AND f.RequestTypeNew NOT IN (5, 20, 22, 26, 30, 50)
  AND f.Assignedtoint IN (14, 20, 23, 25, 70)
  AND f.datecleared >= DATEADD(DAY, -@PERIOD_DAYS, GETDATE())
```

